  "_calib": "FK MODE. Every limb rests pointing straight DOWN (0,0,-1). All FK_* bones: X NEGATIVE swings FORWARD (+Y), X positive swings back; Z NEGATIVE swings to the character's LEFT (-X), Z positive to its RIGHT (+X). Exactly 1:1 in degrees, and IDENTICAL on both sides - no mirror inversion. Y is roll about the limb axis. Lower-limb angles are RELATIVE to the parent, so a bent knee is LowerLeg X positive against a forward thigh. TORSO/UpTorso rot: X+ leans BACK, Y twists (+ turns toward the character's left), Z leans sideways. ROOT loc: X and Y inverted, Z 1:1 up.",
  "_design": "30fps and 0.8s because that is what Roblox actually is: the Animation Editor defaults to 30fps and a combat move runs 0.3-0.7s. The five poses are the standard beat set - idle, anticipation, contact, follow-through, recovery. Easing is per segment: accelerate INTO the strike, decelerate out of it. Angles are deliberately exaggerated past human range, which is what real Roblox combat animation looks like.",
